NAME
       mkfifo - make named pipes

SYNOPSIS
       mkfifo [-m MODE] NAME...

DESCRIPTION
       A named pipe (FIFO) is a special file that connects two programs:
       what one writes into it, the other reads out, in order. ls -l shows it
       with the type letter p. Nothing is stored on disk.

OPTIONS
       -m, --mode MODE
              Set the permissions of the pipe.

EXAMPLES
           mkfifo /tmp/pipe1
           ls -l /tmp/pipe1

SEE ALSO
       mknod(1), find(1)
